        "text": "=TICKET CONTEXT:\n- Ticket ID: {{ $json.ticket_id }}\n- Customer: {{ $json.Name }} ({{ $json.Email }})\n- Subject: {{ $json.Subject }}\n- Category: {{ $json.Category }}\n- Urgency: {{ $json.Urgency }}\n- Sentiment: {{ $json.Sentiment }}\n- Confidence: {{ $json.Confidence }}\n- Summary: {{ $json.Summary }}\n\nCUSTOMER MESSAGE:\n{{ $json.Message }}\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Query the vector store and use EXACTLY the top 3 most relevant chunks (no more, no less)\n2. Draft a professional customer reply using the retrieved knowledge\n3. Match the tone to the customer sentiment ({{ $json.Sentiment }})\n4. Reference specific knowledge base articles/policies by name when found (IMPORTANT: ALWAYS cite the filename from the metadata of retrieved chunks, e.g., '[Source: filename.md]')\n5. Treat retrieval as low-confidence when top similarity score is below 0.45 OR no relevant chunks are returned; in that case add this note at the end: 'Note: No specific policy found — this response is based on general knowledge.'\n\nReturn ONLY the draft email response text.",
